# A corpus is what a score is taken over, and it is not carried by this repository: a format's own
# files are megabytes each, several per pattern, and a repository that carried one set per format
# would be a repository nobody clones.
#
# What is carried is the two small files that make a corpus a record rather than a directory of
# pictures: what it is and how it was made (`policy.toml`), and what a measurement over it came to
# (`SCORE.md`). Everything else here is local — made again with `./run.sh chunker --capture <format>`,
# or pointed at with `--corpus <dir>` when it is somebody's own files.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!*/policy.toml
!*/SCORE.md
